<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">November Uprising</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1830–1831</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The November Uprising was a Polish revolt against Russian rule in Congress <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> that began in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw">Warsaw</a> on 29 November 1830 with an attack by officer cadets on the Belweder Palace. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sejm">Sejm</a> deposed Nicholas I as king of Poland in January 1831, but the Polish army was defeated and Warsaw fell in September 1831. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> abolished the kingdom's constitution, and thousands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poles">Poles</a> left in the Great Emigration.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/november-uprising.jpg" alt="November Uprising" width="320" height="203" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marcin Zaleski · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marcin_Zaleski,_Wzi%C4%99cie_Arsena%C5%82u.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
